HST Office: HST_RIBBON_DUMP_WIDTHS writes the measured width of every ribbon group state, for tuning the collapse chain.

Ribbon 1.0.2 plan (phase 0): the collapse chain of the approved mockup is replayed offline with the real widths of the
groups on Linux and Windows. With the environment variable set, every layout of a ribbon tab box writes one line to
stderr: box, width, chevron, DPI factor, whether the tab has its own ladder, each group's widths at L, M, S (and its
button), a gallery's without the previews the box reserves for it (marked "*"), the state chosen, the row width, the
overflow count and the priority. Without the variable nothing changes.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/vcl/source/control/PriorityMergedHBox.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/control/PriorityMergedHBox.cxx
@@ -39,6 +39,9 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <rtl/strbuf.hxx>
 #include <vcl/event.hxx>
 #include <vcl/image.hxx>
 #include <vcl/toolbox.hxx>
@@ -550,6 +553,46 @@
         m_aHstLastStates = aLayout.states;
         m_nHstLastWidth = nWidth;
